IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `colc-common`

-- Emergency Services Funding Act 1998 (SA), ss 3, 15, 16, with the Emergency Services Funding (Remissions--Land)
-- Regulations 2014, regs 3, 5A, 6, 7, 8 -- the seat-neutral core for the emergency services levy on a home: who is the
-- owner and liable, the notice and its dates, the general remission, the concession holders' remission and the further
-- $46, and the duty to pay by the date in the notice.
--
-- ACTORS (the text's own): the owner of land, co-owners, a married couple or domestic partnership, the Commissioner
-- (of State Taxation), the Minister. The concession holder's questions are in colc-seat.l4.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Act: s 3(1) ("owner of land", paragraphs (a), (e), (f)), s 15(1)-(2) (liability; co-owners
-- jointly and severally liable), s 16(1)-(3) (notice of levy; the payment date at least 28 days after service; service
-- on one co-owner). Regulations: reg 3 ("residential land", "relevant financial year",
-- "domestic partner", "prescribed rate"), reg 5A (general remission), reg 6 (concession holders), reg 7(1a), (2), (3)
-- (amounts), reg 8 (order of deduction).
--
-- THE MISSING FORMULAS. reg 7(1a) and reg 7(2) each say the amount "is determined in accordance with the following
-- formula:" and the formula did not survive into the corpus text (see
-- ../../../emergency-services-funding-remissions-land-regulations-2014/registers/source-bundle/emergency-services-funding-remissions-land-regulations-2014.formulas.md:
-- "not transcribed"). reg 7(2)'s "where" list survives: "A is the amount of the remission; L1 is the amount of the
-- component of the levy that is based on the value of the land; PR is the prescribed rate." Both amounts are INPUTS
-- here (the amount for the whole land, as the notice of levy would show it); neither is guessed.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 15(3)-(6) (a subsequent owner's liability for a levy left unpaid, and the rights of recovery that go
-- with it); the levy itself and its declaration (ss 5-10: capital value, area and land use factors), the assessment
-- book (ss 12-14), refunds, interest and penalty levy (ss 17-17M), recovery and collection (ss 17N-22M), the levy on
-- vehicles and vessels (Part 3 Division 2); s 3(1) paragraphs (b)-(d) (dedicated and unalienated Crown land, owned by
-- a Minister, body or the Crown) and the "arrogated" owner; s 5(10) (residential land held from the South Australian
-- Housing Trust is exempt); regulations 5 (Crown-land occupiers), 8A-20 (residential parks, rural, regional, other land
-- uses, subsequent owners' remission, public land tenants, private roads). Crown-land occupiers answer `not covered`.
--
-- EDITION. Act: Open Australian Legal Corpus text as at 2023-11-25 (scraped 2024-09-13; the Current Titles list of
-- 22 September 2026 listed a later version, 4.12.2025), deposited at
-- ../../../emergency-services-funding-act-1998/registers/source-bundle/emergency-services-funding-act-1998.txt.
-- Regulations: corpus text as at 2024-07-01 (scraped 2024-09-13), deposited at
-- ../../../emergency-services-funding-remissions-land-regulations-2014/registers/source-bundle/emergency-services-funding-remissions-land-regulations-2014.txt.
--
-- COVERAGE. reg 3: "relevant financial year means the 2024/2025 financial year", and each remission is of "the levy ...
-- for the relevant financial year". Any other year answers `not covered`.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- from the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0); each text is as at the corpus scrape and may be out of date.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Emergency Services Funding Act 1998 and Remissions--Land Regulations 2014 -- the core`

§§ `s 3(1) -- the owner of land`

-- s 3(1): "owner of land means (a) where the land has been granted in fee simple (i) in the case of land that is subject
-- to a life estate--the holder of the life estate; (ii) in any other case--the holder of the estate in fee simple in the
-- land; ... (e) where the land is held from the Crown under lease, licence or agreement to purchase (i) if the lease,
-- licence or agreement confers a right to occupy the land--the person entitled to the right of occupation; (ii) in any
-- other case--the Crown; (f) where the land is held under a shack lease--the person entitled to the right of
-- occupation". A tenant under a residential tenancy agreement holds none of these and is not the owner (INFERENCE from
-- the list).
DECLARE `Interest in land` IS ONE OF
    `the holder of the estate in fee simple, the land not being subject to a life estate`
    `the holder of a life estate in land granted in fee simple`
    `the holder of the estate in fee simple in land subject to another person's life estate`
    `the person entitled to occupy land held from the Crown under a lease, licence or agreement to purchase`
    `the person entitled to occupy land held under a shack lease`
    `a tenant or other occupier holding none of these interests`

GIVEN `i` IS AN `Interest in land`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holder of that interest is the owner of the land` `i` IF
        `i` EQUALS `the holder of the estate in fee simple, the land not being subject to a life estate`
    OR  `i` EQUALS `the holder of a life estate in land granted in fee simple`
    OR  `i` EQUALS `the person entitled to occupy land held from the Crown under a lease, licence or agreement to purchase`
    OR  `i` EQUALS `the person entitled to occupy land held under a shack lease`

§§ `s 15(1), (2), s 16 -- liability for the levy and the notice of levy`

-- One owner's (or would-be owner's) position on the land, for the relevant financial year.
-- reg 6(1)(c): the person falls within a reg 6(5) class "(i) on the date of issue stated in the notice of levy ...; or
-- (ii) on the date by which the levy must be paid stated in the notice ...; or (iii) at any time between the dates
-- referred to in subparagraphs (i) and (ii)" -- one FACT, as the text joins the three.
-- reg 6(6): "land comprises a person's principal place of residence if the Minister is satisfied that it comprised the
-- person's principal place of residence on 1 July of the financial year to which the levy relates": the Minister's
-- satisfaction is an INPUT, answered conditionally.
DECLARE `Owner of the home` HAS
    `interest at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` IS AN `Interest in land`
    `share of the land` IS A NUMBER
    `card or payment` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`
    `falls within a class on the date of issue, on the payment date or at any time between` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied the land was the principal place of residence on 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 15(1): "The person who is the owner of land at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July in the financial year for which a levy has been
-- declared is liable to pay the levy to the Commissioner." Only this primary liability is encoded: s 15(3), under which
-- "A subsequent owner of land is liable for a levy, or a part of a levy, in respect of that land that has not been paid
-- by the person or persons primarily liable", is not (finding 23).
GIVEN `o` IS AN `Owner of the home`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is liable for the levy` `o` IF
    `the holder of that interest is the owner of the land` (`o`'s `interest at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July`)

-- s 15(2): "Two or more persons who own the same land are jointly and severally liable for the levy in respect of that
-- land and are entitled to contribution between each other in proportion to the value of their respective interests
-- in the land." So the Commissioner may look to any one co-owner for the whole levy; as between the co-owners, each
-- bears a share. READING: the share of the value is taken to be the share of the land.
GIVEN `the levy` IS A NUMBER, `o` IS AN `Owner of the home`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the Commissioner can recover from one owner` `the levy` `o` MEANS
    IF `the owner is liable for the levy` `o` THEN `the levy` ELSE 0

-- s 16(1): "The Commissioner must serve notice of the amount of the levy that is payable in respect of land for a
-- financial year on the person who was the owner of the land at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July in that year." (2): "The notice
-- must state (a) the amount of the levy; (b) the area factor and the land use factor applicable to the land; (c) the
-- capital value of the land; (d) the date (being at least 28 days after the notice is served) by which the levy must be
-- paid; ..." (3): "Where there are two or more owners of land, service of the notice on one of them will be taken to be
-- service on both or all of them." The Commissioner's duty is encoded for what it means to the owner: the payment
-- date can be no earlier than 28 days after service.
`the least number of days between service and the payment date` MEANS 28

GIVEN `the date the notice was served` IS A DATE, `the date by which the levy must be paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment date is at least 28 days after the notice was served` `the date the notice was served` `the date by which the levy must be paid` IF
    `days from` `the date the notice was served` `to` `the date by which the levy must be paid` AT LEAST `the least number of days between service and the payment date`

§§ `reg 3 -- residential land and the relevant financial year`

-- reg 3: "relevant financial year means the 2024/2025 financial year".
GIVEN `the year it begins` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the relevant financial year` `the year it begins` IF
    `the year it begins` EQUALS 2024

-- The land and its notice of levy. reg 3: "residential land means land that is taken under section 8(2) of the Act to
-- be used for the purpose defined as residential in that section" -- the land use on the notice: a FACT.
DECLARE `Land under the notice of levy` HAS
    `the levy's financial year begins in` IS A NUMBER
    `the land is residential land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount of the levy` IS A NUMBER
    `the regulation 7(2) remission for the land` IS A NUMBER
    `the regulation 7(1a) remission for the land` IS A NUMBER

§§ `reg 6 -- the concession holders' remission`

-- reg 6(5): "To be entitled to a remission under this regulation, a person must be (a) the holder of a current Pensioner
-- Concession Card ...; (b) ... TPI Gold Repatriation Health Card ...; (c) ... War Widows Gold Repatriation Health Card
-- ...; (d) ... Gold Repatriation Health Card (EDA) ...; (e) ... Gold Repatriation Health Card issued ... to a person
-- with 80 or more overall impairment points under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 ...; (f) ...
-- Commonwealth Seniors Health Card ...; (g) ... Low Income Health Care Card ...; (h) in receipt of (i) an Austudy
-- payment; or (ii) a jobseeker payment; or (iii) a parenting payment; or (vi) a special benefit; or (viii) a youth
-- allowance, under the Social Security Act 1991 of the Commonwealth; or (i) in receipt of an Abstudy payment ...; or
-- (j) in receipt of payments under the Community Development Program ...; or (k) in receipt of payments under the
-- Self-Employment Allowance established by the Commonwealth Government; or (l) in receipt of a pension as a war widow
-- under legislation of the United Kingdom or New Zealand; or (n) in receipt of farm household allowance payments under
-- the Farm Household Support Act 2014 of the Commonwealth." There is no (m). (k) is read as the Self-Employment
-- Assistance allowance (finding 10).
GIVEN `c` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a class set out in regulation 6(5)` `c` IF
        `c` EQUALS `a Pensioner Concession Card`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a TPI Gold Repatriation Health Card`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a War Widows Gold Repatriation Health Card`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a Gold Repatriation Health Card (EDA)`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a Gold Repatriation Health Card issued for 80 or more impairment points under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a Low Income Health Care Card`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `an Austudy payment`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a JobSeeker payment`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a parenting payment`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a special benefit`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a youth allowance`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `an Abstudy payment`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `payments under the Community Development Program`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `Self-Employment Assistance allowance payments`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `a war widow's pension under the law of the United Kingdom or New Zealand`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `farm household allowance payments under the Farm Household Support Act 2014`

-- reg 6(1): "If (a) a person holds residential land; and (b) the land comprises his or her principal place of
-- residence; and (c) he or she falls within 1 or more of the classes set out in subregulation (5)" in the window, "the
-- levy in respect of that land for the relevant financial year is remitted for the benefit of that person to the extent
-- set out in regulation 7(2)". READING: "holds" is read as being the owner (and so liable) under s 3(1) and s 15(1)
-- (finding 13).
GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`, `o` IS AN `Owner of the home`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission in their own right` `l` `o` IF
        `is the relevant financial year` (`l`'s `the levy's financial year begins in`)
    AND `l`'s `the land is residential land`
    AND `the owner is liable for the levy` `o`
    AND `o`'s `the Minister is satisfied the land was the principal place of residence on 1 July`
    AND `is a class set out in regulation 6(5)` (`o`'s `card or payment`)
    AND `o`'s `falls within a class on the date of issue, on the payment date or at any time between`

-- The owner asking and a spouse or domestic partner who co-owns the land. Whether some other co-owner is entitled to
-- the reg 6 remission is not a field: under the reading in finding 14 the general remission falls to each owner not
-- entitled under reg 6 in proportion to their share whether or not another co-owner is entitled (reg 5A(3), or reg
-- 5A(1) with s 15(2)), and reg 6(3) gives each entitled owner a part for their own share, so no answer turns on it.
DECLARE `Owners of the home` HAS
    `the owner asking` IS AN `Owner of the home`
    `a spouse or domestic partner co-owns the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse or domestic partner` IS AN `Owner of the home`

-- reg 6(4): "If a married couple or domestic partnership owns land solely, or jointly or as tenants in common with
-- another person or persons, the 2 persons comprising the married couple or domestic partnership are entitled to a
-- remission, or a proportionate part of a remission, under this regulation if (a) the land is the principal place of
-- residence of both of them; and (b) either 1 of them is entitled to a remission in respect of the land under this
-- regulation." READING: the couple "owns" the land only where both are owners (finding 13).
GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`, `h` IS AN `Owners of the home`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `regulation 6(4) applies to the couple` `l` `h` IF
        `h`'s `a spouse or domestic partner co-owns the land`
    AND `the owner is liable for the levy` (`h`'s `the owner asking`)
    AND `the owner is liable for the levy` (`h`'s `the spouse or domestic partner`)
    AND (`h`'s `the owner asking`)'s `the Minister is satisfied the land was the principal place of residence on 1 July`
    AND (`h`'s `the spouse or domestic partner`)'s `the Minister is satisfied the land was the principal place of residence on 1 July`
    AND (    `the owner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission in their own right` `l` (`h`'s `the owner asking`)
         OR  `the owner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission in their own right` `l` (`h`'s `the spouse or domestic partner`))

GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`, `h` IS AN `Owners of the home`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner asking is entitled to the regulation 6 remission` `l` `h` IF
        `the owner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission in their own right` `l` (`h`'s `the owner asking`)
    OR  `regulation 6(4) applies to the couple` `l` `h`

GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`, `h` IS AN `Owners of the home`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the spouse or domestic partner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission` `l` `h` IF
        `h`'s `a spouse or domestic partner co-owns the land`
    AND (    `the owner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission in their own right` `l` (`h`'s `the spouse or domestic partner`)
         OR  `regulation 6(4) applies to the couple` `l` `h`)

§§ `reg 7, reg 8 -- the amounts`

-- reg 7(2): the reg 6(1) remission for the land (formula missing: INPUT). READING: it cannot exceed the levy.
GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the regulation 6(1) remission for the land` `l` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`l`'s `the regulation 7(2) remission for the land`) `and` (`l`'s `the amount of the levy`)

-- reg 7(3): "The amount of the remission under regulation 6(2) is $46."
`the further remission in regulation 7(3)` MEANS 46

-- reg 6(2): "a person entitled to a remission under subregulation (1) is entitled to a further remission of the levy in
-- respect of that land to the extent set out in regulation 7(3)". reg 8: "the remission under regulation 6(1) must be
-- determined and deducted before the remission under regulation 6(2) is deducted." READING: the further $46 is
-- deducted from what is left after the reg 6(1) remission, and so cannot take the levy below nil (finding 12).
GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the regulation 6(2) remission for the land` `l` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `the further remission in regulation 7(3)` `and` (`l`'s `the amount of the levy` MINUS `the regulation 6(1) remission for the land` `l`)

GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the concession holders' remission for the whole land` `l` MEANS
    `the regulation 6(1) remission for the land` `l` PLUS `the regulation 6(2) remission for the land` `l`

-- reg 5A(1): "the levy for the relevant financial year in respect of residential land is remitted for the benefit of all
-- persons who are liable to pay the levy in respect of that land to the extent set out in regulation 7" (7(1a), formula
-- missing: INPUT). (2): a person entitled under reg 6, 8A or 10A "is not entitled to a remission in respect of the same
-- land under subregulation (1)". (3): "If 2 or more persons own land jointly or as tenants in common and 1 or more of
-- them is entitled to a remission under regulation 6, the persons who are not entitled to the remission under
-- regulation 6 are entitled to a remission under subregulation (1) proportionate to their interest in the land."
GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the general remission for the whole land` `l` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`l`'s `the regulation 7(1a) remission for the land`) `and` (`l`'s `the amount of the levy`)

-- reg 6(3): "if 2 or more persons own land jointly or as tenants in common, each of them who is entitled to a remission
-- under this regulation in respect of the land is entitled to a part of the remission set out in regulation 7 that is
-- proportionate to his or her interest in the land." The answers below are for the owner asking and, where reg 6(4)
-- or co-ownership brings them in, the spouse or domestic partner: each share of the land carries either its part of the
-- reg 6 remission or its part of the reg 5A remission. A sole owner's share is 1. READING: where no owner is entitled
-- under reg 6, each owner's part of the general remission is also taken in proportion to the share (finding 14).
GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`, `h` IS AN `Owners of the home`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shares carrying the concession holders' remission` `l` `h` MEANS
    `asker's share` PLUS `spouse's share`
    WHERE
        `asker's share` MEANS
            IF `the owner asking is entitled to the regulation 6 remission` `l` `h`
            THEN (`h`'s `the owner asking`)'s `share of the land`
            ELSE 0
        `spouse's share` MEANS
            IF `the spouse or domestic partner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission` `l` `h`
            THEN (`h`'s `the spouse or domestic partner`)'s `share of the land`
            ELSE 0

GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`, `h` IS AN `Owners of the home`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shares carrying the general remission` `l` `h` MEANS
    `asker's share` PLUS `spouse's share`
    WHERE
        `asker's share` MEANS
            IF      `the owner is liable for the levy` (`h`'s `the owner asking`)
                AND (NOT (`the owner asking is entitled to the regulation 6 remission` `l` `h`))
            THEN (`h`'s `the owner asking`)'s `share of the land`
            ELSE 0
        `spouse's share` MEANS
            IF      `h`'s `a spouse or domestic partner co-owns the land`
                AND `the owner is liable for the levy` (`h`'s `the spouse or domestic partner`)
                AND (NOT (`the spouse or domestic partner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission` `l` `h`))
            THEN (`h`'s `the spouse or domestic partner`)'s `share of the land`
            ELSE 0

DECLARE `Why the levy question is not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the deposited regulations remit the levy for the 2024/2025 financial year only`
    `the land is not residential land, and the remissions for other land are not encoded`
    `the land is held from the Crown, and regulation 5 is not encoded`

DECLARE `Levy remission` IS ONE OF
    `the levy remitted for us` HAS
        `under regulations 6 and 7(2), (3)` IS A NUMBER
        `under regulations 5A and 7(1a)` IS A NUMBER
    `no remission: not the owner at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July, so not liable for the levy`
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why the levy question is not covered`

GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`, `h` IS AN `Owners of the home`
GIVETH A `Levy remission`
`the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `l` `h` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`is the relevant financial year` (`l`'s `the levy's financial year begins in`))
            THEN `not covered` `the deposited regulations remit the levy for the 2024/2025 financial year only`
        IF NOT (`l`'s `the land is residential land`)
            THEN `not covered` `the land is not residential land, and the remissions for other land are not encoded`
        IF (`h`'s `the owner asking`)'s `interest at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` EQUALS `the person entitled to occupy land held from the Crown under a lease, licence or agreement to purchase`
            THEN `not covered` `the land is held from the Crown, and regulation 5 is not encoded`
        IF NOT (`the owner is liable for the levy` (`h`'s `the owner asking`))
            THEN `no remission: not the owner at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July, so not liable for the levy`
        OTHERWISE `the levy remitted for us` `concession part` `general part`
    WHERE
        `concession part` MEANS `the shares carrying the concession holders' remission` `l` `h` TIMES `the concession holders' remission for the whole land` `l`
        `general part` MEANS `the shares carrying the general remission` `l` `h` TIMES `the general remission for the whole land` `l`

GIVEN `r` IS A `Levy remission`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total remitted` `r` MEANS
    CONSIDER `r`
    WHEN `the levy remitted for us` `six` `five A` THEN `six` PLUS `five A`
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 15(2): as between co-owners, the owner asking (with a co-owning spouse or partner) bears the levy in proportion to
-- their shares, less what is remitted for them. For a sole owner, the levy less the remissions.
GIVEN `l` IS A `Land under the notice of levy`, `h` IS AN `Owners of the home`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`our share of the levy after the remissions` `l` `h` MEANS
    (`our shares` TIMES `l`'s `the amount of the levy`) MINUS `the total remitted` (`the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `l` `h`)
    WHERE
        `asker's share` MEANS
            IF `the owner is liable for the levy` (`h`'s `the owner asking`)
            THEN (`h`'s `the owner asking`)'s `share of the land`
            ELSE 0
        `spouse's share` MEANS
            IF `h`'s `a spouse or domestic partner co-owns the land` AND `the owner is liable for the levy` (`h`'s `the spouse or domestic partner`)
            THEN (`h`'s `the spouse or domestic partner`)'s `share of the land`
            ELSE 0
        `our shares` MEANS `asker's share` PLUS `spouse's share`

§§ `Regulative rule -- paying the levy`

DECLARE `Levy party` IS ONE OF `the owner of the land`, `the Commissioner`

DECLARE `Levy act` IS ONE OF
    `pay the levy to the Commissioner` HAS `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER

-- s 15(1): the owner "is liable to pay the levy to the Commissioner"; s 16(2)(d): the notice states "the date ... by
-- which the levy must be paid". Clock: days from service of the notice. LEST: interest and penalty levy (ss 17J-17M)
-- and recovery as a debt (s 17O) follow; they are not encoded.
GIVEN `the amount payable` IS A NUMBER, `the days from service to the payment date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Levy party` `Levy act`
DECIDE `s 15(1), s 16(2)(d) -- the owner must pay the levy by the date in the notice` `the amount payable` `the days from service to the payment date` IS
    PARTY `the owner of the land`
    MUST  `pay the levy to the Commissioner` (EXACTLY `the amount payable`)
    WITHIN `the days from service to the payment date`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the owner of the land` BECAUSE "s 15(1), s 16(2)(d): the levy must be paid to the Commissioner by the date stated in the notice of levy; interest and penalty levy under ss 17J-17M and recovery as a debt under s 17O are not encoded"
